All done. Summary of what was performed:

## Change
In `/etc/nginx/nginx.conf`, the only modification was in the `server` block:
```diff
-        ssl_verify_client on;
+        ssl_verify_client off;
```

## Validation & reload
- `nginx -t -c /etc/nginx/nginx.conf` → *syntax is ok / test is successful*
- `nginx -s reload -c /etc/nginx/nginx.conf` → graceful reload; master process (PID 16) kept running with a new worker, so the loopback HTTPS service never went down.

## Final configuration (`/etc/nginx/nginx.conf`)
```nginx
user www-data;
worker_processes 1;
pid /run/nginx.pid;
error_log /tmp/inventory-nginx-error.log notice;

events {
    worker_connections 512;
}

http {
    access_log /tmp/inventory-nginx-access.log;
    keepalive_timeout 10;

    server {
        listen 127.0.0.1:8443 ssl;
        server_name localhost;

        ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;
        ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/tls/server.crt;
        ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/tls/server.key;
        ssl_client_certificate /etc/nginx/tls/ca.crt;
        ssl_verify_client off;

        location = /health {
            root /srv/inventory;
            try_files /health.json =404;
            default_type application/json;
        }
    }
}
```

## Probe results (trusting `/etc/nginx/tls/ca.crt`)
| Probe | Command essence | Result |
|---|---|---|
| With trusted client cert | `curl --cacert ca.crt --cert client.crt --key client.key https://127.0.0.1:8443/health` | **HTTP 200** — `{"status":"ok"}` |
| Without client cert | `curl --cacert ca.crt https://127.0.0.1:8443/health` | **HTTP 200** — `{"status":"ok"}` |

Before the change, the no-cert probe returned `400` (baseline verification of the original `on` setting). Both probes now return 200, and nginx continues serving HTTPS on `127.0.0.1:8443`.
